West Elk and Sawatch Mountains; Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5d9a0ec4f46df7deb3c2c0e5015df58147db243f.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5d9a0ec4f46df7deb3c2c0e5015df58147db243f.001.1"},{"event":"Winter Storm Warning","headline":"Winter Storm Warning issued October 31 at 10:37AM MDT until November 2 at 12:00PM MST by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Heavy snow expected above 10, 000 feet. Total snow\naccumulations between 12 and 18 inches, with locally higher amounts\npossible. Winds gusting as high as 45 mph.\n\n* WHERE...Northwest San Juan Mountains and Southwest San Juan\nMountains.\n\n* WHEN...From 6 AM Sunday to noon MST Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Travel could be very difficult to impossible. The\nhazardous conditions will impact the Monday morning commute.","ends":"2026-11-02T12:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.2bdd41b860e09ab541155db973dc91e9b1c8543e.001.2","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.2bdd41b860e09ab541155db973dc91e9b1c8543e.001.2"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 31 at 9:50AM MDT until November 2 at 11:00AM MST by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"...The National Weather Service in Grand Junction CO has issued a\nFlood Warning for the following rivers in Colorado...\n\nLa Plata River at Hesperus affecting La Plata County.\n\nFor the La Plata River...including Hesperus...Minor flooding is\nforecast.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov/gjt.\n\nThe next statement will be issued Monday morning at 900 AM MST.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is forecast. This approaches the flood of\nrecord.\n\n* WHERE...La Plata River at Hesperus.\n\n* WHEN...From Sunday afternoon to Monday morning.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 9:30 AM MDT Saturday the stage was 4.1 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 5.0 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to rise above flood stage Sunday\nevening to a crest of 5.8 feet late Sunday evening. It will then\nfall below flood stage early Monday morning.\n- Flood stage is 5.5 feet.\n- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 5.8\nfeet on 05/21/2005.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-11-02T11:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"La Plata, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.516514de7fcd1a54cf04b8b0f74cfdb0cdac2c19.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.516514de7fcd1a54cf04b8b0f74cfdb0cdac2c19.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued October 30 at 3:02PM MDT until November 2 at 11:00AM MST by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of southwest Colorado, including the following\nareas, Animas River Basin, Four Corners/Upper Dolores River, San\nJuan River Basin and Southwest San Juan Mountains and southeast\nUtah, including the following areas, Canyonlands/Natural Bridges,\nLa Sal and Abajo Mountains and Southeast Utah.\n\n* WHEN...From late Saturday night through Monday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, recently burned areas, and other low-lying and\nflood-prone locations. Low-water crossings may be flooded. Storm\ndrains and ditches may become clogged with debris.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- 1 to 3 inches of rain is expected across portions of southeast\nUtah and southwest Colorado from Sunday morning through Monday\nmorning over soils that are still saturated from recent rainfall\nand flooding.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-11-02T11:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Southwest San Juan Mountains; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin; Southeast Utah; La Sal and Abaj